

From: Kyrylo Tkachov <ktkachov@nvidia.com>

Late vsetvl PRE can insert a configuration on an edge from a shared
jump-table dispatch.  Such an edge cannot be split for one dispatch
without also changing the other users of the table.

Keep the local configuration in blocks with incoming shared-table edges,
using the existing invalid_opt_bb_p check.

RISC-V shares jump tables, and without this patch the new test fails with
an ICE in rtl_split_edge.  With it, the test passes at VLEN 128 and 256.
The test also checks that its dispatches share their tables.

Jeff approved v3 of this patch (6/7), provided that the patches it
depends on are approved:
https://inbox.sourceware.org/gcc-patches/5191ab1c-37af-4345-a6f9-0cb551b98439@oss.qualcomm.com/

gcc/ChangeLog:

	PR middle-end/126236
	* config/riscv/riscv-vsetvl.cc (invalid_opt_bb_p): Keep local
	configurations in blocks with incoming shared-table edges.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	PR middle-end/126236
	* gcc.target/riscv/rvv/vsetvl/pr126236.c: New test.

Signed-off-by: Kyrylo Tkachov <ktkachov@nvidia.com>
---
Changes since v3:
- RISC-V now shares jump tables, so the shared-table check has an
  effect.  TARGET_CAN_SHARE_JUMP_TABLE_P defaults to true (patch 3), and
  patch 4 does not opt RISC-V out.  In v3, only AArch64 shared tables.
- invalid_opt_bb_p now calls shared_tablejump_p, a new helper from
  patch 2, instead of tablejump_p and JUMP_TABLE_SHARED_P.  The
  condition does not change.
- gcc.target/riscv/rvv/vsetvl/pr126236.c now uses -fdump-rtl-compgotos.
  Two new scan-rtl-dump checks fail if compgotos copies no dispatch or
  if no jump table has the shared flag (/u).  Both skip -flto runs.
- The commit message now says that pr126236.c fails with an ICE in
  rtl_split_edge without the fix.  v3 used an audit-only hook to get the
  ICE and said that the test did not exercise table sharing by default.

